 "cost_total_hnsw_4": "12.3",
 "cost_flows_per_s_hnsw": "81,000",
 "cost_knn_ratio": "5",
 "resp_cost": "On four threads, LightGBM inference takes 4.7 µs per flow, exact kNN scoring against the 20,000-flow reference 23.3 µs and the conformal and Fisher step 0.29 µs, so exact kNN search, not the detector, dominates the cost of the layer. It grows linearly with the reference (128.2 µs per flow at 100,000 flows). An approximate HNSW index brings it down to 7.3 µs at 20,000 flows and 9.1 µs at 100,000 flows, with top-5 neighbour recall between 0.867 and 0.983; tree indexes are slower than brute-force search on these 77 features.",
